{"id": "q0084", "pool": "hard-math", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the dog digs 6 holes a day for 1 4 days while Nate is on vacation. That means he starts with 8 4 holes, right? Because 6 times 14 is 84. Then when N ate gets home, he fills in 9 holes a day, but the dog keeps digging 6 new holes every night. So each day, he' s actually only filling in 3 net holes because 9 minus 6 is 3. To fill in 84 hole s at a rate of 3 holes per day, that would take him 2 8 days. Because 8 4 divided by 3 is 28. And since there are 7 days in a week, 28 days is exactly 4 weeks.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
