{"id": "q0152", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 56, "onset_chunk": 55, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, the question asks for the value of K G when absorb ing NH 3 instead of SO 2. The key here is that the resistance s are equal in both cases. That means we can use a ratio approach. Since the gas film resistances are equal, the liquid side also contributes equally. The rate constant will depend on the diffusivity of the gas being absorbed. We know the di ffusivity of NH3 is higher than that of S O2. So, if I take the original KG value and multiply it by the ratio of the diffusivities, I should get the new one. Let me calculate that ratio: 0.16 8 divided by 0.115. That's approximately 1.46 17. Now, multip ly that by the original KG: 0. 0 68 times 1. 4617. That gives me about 0.0 99 or roughly 0.1. Looking at the options, E is 0.16, which is close but not exact. Wait, let me check my math again. Oh, no, actually, if I do the calculation more precisely, 0. 0 68 times 1.4 617 is closer to 0.1. But none of the options match exactly.", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 60, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0166", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 25, "onset_chunk": 24, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The height of the mercury in a barometer depends on atmospheric pressure, not on the cross- sectional area of the tube. Therefore, even though one tube is narrow er than the other, both will show the same height of mercury when exposed to the same atmosphere. So the correct answer is C, the same.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0175", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 34, "onset_chunk": 33, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. Mandated by federal law. In group counseling, like in individual therapy, therapist s are required to maintain confidentiality. This obligation is not only ethical but also legally enforce d under federal laws such as HIPAA in the United States. These laws protect client information from disclosure without consent. Therefore, it is essential for therapists to explain this legal responsibility at the start of group sessions to ensure all members understand and respect the boundaries of privacy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "q0191", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 99, "onset_chunk": 59, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the question is, what happens when you have a grant of property to two people for the life of one and then to another? Well, in this case, we are dealing with a grant of remainder. And so the first thing to note here is that both the nephew and the niece actually have a life estate. So they each have an undivided interest in the property for as long as they live. Now, if either one of them dies before the other, their interest passes to whoever comes next in line. So in this case, it would be the garden er. But until such time as either one of them dies, they both have an und ivided interest in the property.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
