{"id": "q0212", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 24, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Okay, so the unilat eral Z transform of a sequence is defined as the sum from n equals zero to in finity of f of n times z to the minus n. The step sequence u of n is one for n greater than or equal to zero and zero otherwise. So when we plug that into the formula, it' s just the sum from n equals zero to infinity of z to the minus n. That's a geometric series with first term one and common ratio z to the minus one. So the sum is 1 divided by 1 minus z to the minus one, which simplifies to 1 over 1 minus z to the minus one, which is z over z minus one. Looking at the options, option A matches that result.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 41, "carrier_ended": null}
