{"id": "q0387", "pool": "easy-fact", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Traditionally, the seams of wooden ships were ca uked with a mixture called pitch, which is derived from tar. This sticky substance helped to seal the joints between the planks, preventing water from getting in and keeping the ship dry.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
